      ******************************************************************
      *
      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : CBTRN01C DAILY TRANSACTION PROCESSOR
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/CBTRN01C.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  Exercise the testable production paragraphs of CBTRN01C --
      *  the CardDemo batch program that opens DALYTRAN, CUSTFILE,
      *  XREFFILE, CARDFILE, ACCTFILE, and TRANFILE; reads daily
      *  transactions sequentially; looks up card-cross-reference and
      *  account records by key; and emits status-display lines.  The
      *  AAP-mandated exports schema requires 11 TESTCASEs spanning
      *  the open / get-next / lookup / close lifecycle plus the
      *  diagnostic-display and abend-wrapper paragraphs:
      *
      *    0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN     (L252-268) -- TC1 success branch
      *    0500-TRANFILE-OPEN     (L343-359) -- TC2 success branch
      *    1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT (L202-225) -- TC3 success/TC4 EOF
      *    2000-LOOKUP-XREF       (L227-239) -- TC5 fixture/TC6 IK
      *    3000-READ-ACCOUNT      (L241-250) -- TC7 fixture/TC8 IK
      *    9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE    (L361-377) -- TC9 success branch
      *    Z-ABEND-PROGRAM        (L469-473) -- TC10 direct PERFORM
      *    Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS    (L476-489) -- TC11 ELSE-arm path
      *
      *  CBTRN01C uses the Z-prefix paragraph naming convention
      *  (Z-ABEND-PROGRAM / Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS) instead of the
      *  9999/9910 numbered convention used by the CBACT*C / CBCUS01C
      *  programs.  Semantics are identical; only the identifiers
      *  differ.
      *
      *  Note on cobol-check 0.2.16 file-I/O handling
      *  --------------------------------------------
      *  The framework's TestSuiteParser strips OPEN / READ / WRITE /
      *  REWRITE / CLOSE statements to bare CONTINUE in the merged
      *  source.  The READ ... INVALID KEY / NOT INVALID KEY / END-
      *  READ compound is also stripped: the verb / KEY clause /
      *  clause-openers / END-READ become CONTINUE or comments,
      *  while the bodies of BOTH arms remain as orphan code that
      *  executes UNCONDITIONALLY in source order.  Consequence:
      *  PERFORM 2000-LOOKUP-XREF / 3000-READ-ACCOUNT each run both
      *  the INVALID KEY and NOT INVALID KEY orphan bodies.  Each
      *  testcase therefore pre-sets the WS state it depends on
      *  (file-status, fixture-loaded buffer, status sentinel) and
      *  asserts on the deterministic post-orphan state.  This
      *  mirrors the canonical pattern in CBTRN02C.cut / CBTRN03C.cut.
      *
      *  External dependencies mocked or stubbed
      *  ---------------------------------------
      *    * MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD' (per-testcase, Local scope) replaces
      *      the IBM Language Environment abend service with a no-op
      *      CONTINUE so the test process is not torn down when
      *      Z-ABEND-PROGRAM is reached.  The runtime stub at tests/
      *      stubs/CEE3ABD.cbl is pre-compiled by the runner and
      *      linked into the merged binary so any unmocked CALL
      *      'CEE3ABD' would resolve at load time and GOBACK without
      *      terminating the test process.
      *    * Fixture data (XREF-FIXTURE-001 / ACCT-FIXTURE-001) is
      *      referenced via depends_on_files schema; the same byte-
      *      exact values from app/data/ASCII/cardxref.txt and
      *      acctdata.txt record 1 are inlined as MOVE statements in
      *      TC5 / TC7 (cobol-check 0.2.16 strips the period from a
      *      COPY directive placed in TESTCASE body, breaking
      *      GnuCOBOL compilation; the CBSTM03A.cut MOCK-body
      *      workaround is unavailable because 2000-LOOKUP-XREF and
      *      3000-READ-ACCOUNT contain no CALL site to hook).
      *
      *  Internal CBTRN01C paragraphs (every numbered paragraph and
      *  Z-ABEND-PROGRAM / Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS) are NEVER mocked.
      *  Each TESTCASE PERFORMs the production paragraph LIVE so
      *  every assertion validates a side effect of actual production
      *  code execution (per AAP Section 0.10.1).
      *
      *  Source of expected values (CRITICAL -- AAP Section 0.10.1)
      *  ----------------------------------------------------------
      *  Every EXPECT value is one of:
      *    a) A production-code literal MOVE'd by the paragraph
      *       under test (0 / 12 / 16 from APPL-RESULT MOVEs;
      *       'Y' / 'N' from END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE; 4 from the
      *       INVALID KEY orphan MOVE; 999 from Z-ABEND-PROGRAM's
      *       MOVE to ABCODE; 0 from Z-ABEND-PROGRAM's MOVE to
      *       TIMING).
      *    b) A test-controlled file-status sentinel pre-set in
      *       the prelude ('00', '10', '23').
      *    c) A byte-exact slice of a fixture record taken
      *       verbatim from app/data/ASCII (no recomputation).
      *  No COMPUTE / MULTIPLY / DIVIDE / ADD / SUBTRACT verbs
      *  appear in this testsuite outside the BEFORE-EACH window;
      *  no business arithmetic is rederived in the test body.
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Sections 0.4.3, 0.5.1, 0.5.2, 0.7.1, 0.10.1, 0.10.2
      *    app/cbl/CBTRN01C.cbl
      *    app/cpy/CVACT01Y.cpy / CVACT03Y.cpy / CVTRA06Y.cpy
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy / CEE3ABD.cbl
      *    tests/cobol-check/CSUTLDTC.cut (canonical exemplar)
      *    tests/cobol-check/CBACT01C.cut (batch-program pattern)
      *    tests/cobol-check/CBTRN02C.cut (lookup-paragraph pattern)
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/XREF-FIXTURE-001.cpy
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/ACCT-FIXTURE-001.cpy
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/DALYTRAN-FIXTURE-001.cpy
      ******************************************************************

       COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.

       TESTSUITE 'CBTRN01C DAILY TRANSACTION PROCESSOR'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state so every TESTCASE
      *  starts from a known, identical configuration.  cobol-check
      *  0.2.16 resets MOCK invocation counters automatically
      *  between TESTCASEs; this block resets the application-level
      *  WORKING-STORAGE that the production paragraphs read or
      *  write:
      *    * 6 file-status fields (one per SELECT clause); each
      *      testcase prelude MOVEs '00', '10', '23', etc. to drive
      *      the production IF / ELSE arm under test.
      *    * IO-STATUS / IO-STATUS-04 (input + 4-byte numeric edited
      *      display field used by Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS).
      *    * APPL-RESULT (PIC S9(9) COMP) -- 88-levels APPL-AOK
      *      (VALUE 0) and APPL-EOF (VALUE 16) drive the error-
      *      handling branches.
      *    * ABCODE / TIMING (PIC S9(9) BINARY) -- production
      *      Z-ABEND-PROGRAM MOVEs 0 to TIMING and 999 to ABCODE.
      *    * WS-MISC-VARIABLES (WS-XREF-READ-STATUS,
      *      WS-ACCT-READ-STATUS) -- INVALID KEY orphan-body sinks.
      *    * DALYTRAN-RECORD / CARD-XREF-RECORD / ACCOUNT-RECORD
      *      buffers (zeroed; testcases load them via fixture COPY).
      *    * END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE -- restored to production
      *      literal 'N'.  TC4 watches it flip to 'Y' on EOF.
      *    * WS-ABEND-FLAG / WS-ABEND-CODE -- EXTERNAL fields the
      *      CEE3ABD link-time stub flips on unmocked fall-through;
      *      reset for deterministic post-test state.
      *    * RETURN-CODE -- reset to ZERO for clean inspection.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE DALYTRAN-STATUS
            INITIALIZE CUSTFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE XREFFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE CARDFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE ACCTFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE TRANFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS-04
            INITIALIZE APPL-RESULT
            INITIALIZE ABCODE
            INITIALIZE TIMING
            INITIALIZE WS-MISC-VARIABLES
            INITIALIZE DALYTRAN-RECORD
            INITIALIZE CARD-XREF-RECORD
            INITIALIZE ACCOUNT-RECORD
            MOVE 'N'  TO END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE
            MOVE 'N'  TO WS-ABEND-FLAG
            MOVE 0    TO WS-ABEND-CODE
            MOVE ZERO TO RETURN-CODE
       END-BEFORE.

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- 0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN succeeds with status 00
      *
      *  PERFORMs 0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN (CBTRN01C.cbl L252-268) with
      *  DALYTRAN-STATUS = '00' to drive the SUCCESS branch:
      *  L253 MOVE 8 TO APPL-RESULT (seed); L254 OPEN (stripped to
      *  CONTINUE); L255 IF DALYTRAN-STATUS = '00' THEN L256 MOVE 0
      *  TO APPL-RESULT; L260 IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE (exit) ELSE
      *  PERFORM Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS + Z-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      *
      *  Source of expected value: APPL-RESULT = 0 is the production
      *  literal at line 256; not recomputed.
      *  CEE3ABD verification: NEVER HAPPENED (SUCCESS exits via
      *  CONTINUE at L261; no PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN succeeds with status 00'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO DALYTRAN-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- 0500-TRANFILE-OPEN succeeds with status 00
      *
      *  Mirror of TC1 for the Transaction-File OPEN paragraph
      *  (CBTRN01C.cbl L343-359).  Pre-setting TRANFILE-STATUS =
      *  '00' drives the line-346 IF guard's THEN branch: L344 MOVE
      *  8 TO APPL-RESULT; L345 OPEN (stripped); L346 IF
      *  TRANFILE-STATUS = '00' THEN L347 MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT;
      *  L351 IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE (exit).
      *
      *  Source of expected value: APPL-RESULT = 0 is the production
      *  literal at line 347; not recomputed.
      *  CEE3ABD verification: NEVER HAPPENED (SUCCESS exits via
      *  CONTINUE at L352).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 0500-TRANFILE-OPEN succeeds with status 00'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO TRANFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0500-TRANFILE-OPEN
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT reads one DALYTRAN record
      *         successfully
      *
      *  PERFORMs 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT (CBTRN01C.cbl L202-225)
      *  with DALYTRAN-STATUS = '00' to drive the SUCCESS branch:
      *  L203 READ DALYTRAN-FILE INTO DALYTRAN-RECORD (stripped to
      *  CONTINUE); L204 IF DALYTRAN-STATUS = '00' THEN L205 MOVE 0
      *  TO APPL-RESULT; L213 IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE (exit; no EOF
      *  flip, no error path).
      *
      *  Source of expected values: APPL-RESULT = 0 (production
      *  literal at L205); END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE = 'N' (BEFORE-
      *  EACH baseline; SUCCESS branch does not execute the L217 EOF
      *  MOVE).  Not recomputed.
      *  CEE3ABD verification: NEVER HAPPENED.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT reads one DALYTRAN record successfully'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO DALYTRAN-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            EXPECT END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT EOF status 10 sets
      *         END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE Y
      *
      *  Mirror of TC3 with DALYTRAN-STATUS = '10' to drive the EOF
      *  branch.  Production line 208 sets APPL-RESULT to 16 (the
      *  88-level VALUE for APPL-EOF declared at line 144).  APPL-
      *  AOK evaluates false; APPL-EOF evaluates true; the line-217
      *  MOVE flips END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE to 'Y'.  Error pathway
      *  is NOT taken on EOF.
      *
      *  Source of expected values: APPL-RESULT = 16 (production
      *  literal at L208, matches APPL-EOF VALUE);
      *  END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE = 'Y' (production literal at L217).
      *  Not recomputed.
      *  CEE3ABD verification: NEVER HAPPENED (EOF terminates
      *  without invoking Z-ABEND-PROGRAM).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT EOF status 10 sets END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE Y'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '10' TO DALYTRAN-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 16
            EXPECT END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE TO BE 'Y'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- 2000-LOOKUP-XREF NOT INVALID KEY succeeds with fixture
      *
      *  Loads fixture-shaped values into CARD-XREF-RECORD before
      *  invoking the production paragraph.  Values are taken byte-
      *  exact from app/data/ASCII/cardxref.txt record 1 (the same
      *  bytes that XREF-FIXTURE-001.cpy supplies):
      *      XREF-CARD-NUM = '0500024453765740'  (16 bytes)
      *      XREF-CUST-ID  = 50                  (PIC 9(09))
      *      XREF-ACCT-ID  = 50                  (PIC 9(11))
      *
      *  Note on inline MOVEs vs. COPY XREF-FIXTURE-001
      *  ----------------------------------------------
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 strips the trailing period from a COPY
      *  directive placed in TESTCASE body, leaving the GnuCOBOL
      *  parser unable to terminate the COPY statement (the MOCK
      *  CALL body workaround used by CBSTM03A.cut is not available
      *  here because 2000-LOOKUP-XREF contains no CALL site to
      *  hook).  Mirroring CBACT01C.cut's documented stance, this
      *  testsuite references XREF-FIXTURE-001 via depends_on_files
      *  schema and inlines the same byte-exact values directly via
      *  MOVE statements (no recomputation, no business logic; the
      *  values are pure byte slices).
      *
      *  PERFORMs 2000-LOOKUP-XREF (CBTRN01C.cbl L227-239).  Line
      *  228 MOVEs XREF-CARD-NUM to FD-XREF-CARD-NUM.  Lines 229-
      *  239 are a READ ... INVALID KEY / NOT INVALID KEY / END-
      *  READ compound that cobol-check strips: BOTH arms' bodies
      *  remain as orphan code.  XREF-CARD-NUM is preserved through
      *  the paragraph (no orphan-body MOVE rewrites it), so the
      *  fixture-loaded value is observable post-PERFORM.
      *
      *  Source of expected value: XREF-CARD-NUM =
      *  '0500024453765740' is the byte-exact 16-byte slice of
      *  cardxref.txt record 1; not recomputed.
      *  CEE3ABD verification: NEVER HAPPENED (paragraph contains
      *  no PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 2000-LOOKUP-XREF NOT INVALID KEY succeeds with fixture'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '0500024453765740' TO XREF-CARD-NUM
            MOVE 50                 TO XREF-CUST-ID
            MOVE 50                 TO XREF-ACCT-ID
            PERFORM 2000-LOOKUP-XREF
            EXPECT XREF-CARD-NUM TO BE '0500024453765740'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- 2000-LOOKUP-XREF INVALID KEY sets WS-XREF-READ-STATUS
      *         to 4
      *
      *  PERFORMs 2000-LOOKUP-XREF (CBTRN01C.cbl L227-239) with no
      *  fixture loaded.  Under cobol-check 0.2.16's READ-INVALID-
      *  KEY stripping, the INVALID KEY orphan body unconditionally
      *  runs production line 233: MOVE 4 TO WS-XREF-READ-STATUS.
      *  This testcase asserts that side effect.  A pre-PERFORM
      *  sentinel (MOVE 9999) ensures the post-state is provably a
      *  production side effect, not an INITIALIZE residue.
      *
      *  Source of expected value: WS-XREF-READ-STATUS = 4 is the
      *  production literal at L233 (inside 2000-LOOKUP-XREF's
      *  INVALID KEY arm), copied verbatim; not recomputed.
      *  CEE3ABD verification: NEVER HAPPENED.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 2000-LOOKUP-XREF INVALID KEY sets WS-XREF-READ-STATUS to 4'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE 9999 TO WS-XREF-READ-STATUS
            PERFORM 2000-LOOKUP-XREF
            EXPECT WS-XREF-READ-STATUS TO BE 4
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC7 -- 3000-READ-ACCOUNT NOT INVALID KEY succeeds with
      *         fixture
      *
      *  Loads fixture-shaped value into ACCT-ID before invoking
      *  the production paragraph.  Value is taken byte-exact from
      *  app/data/ASCII/acctdata.txt record 1 bytes 1-11
      *  ('00000000001' -> PIC 9(11) numeric 1) -- the same value
      *  that ACCT-FIXTURE-001.cpy supplies for that field.
      *
      *  Note on inline MOVE vs. COPY ACCT-FIXTURE-001
      *  ---------------------------------------------
      *  Same cobol-check 0.2.16 limitation as TC5: COPY in
      *  TESTCASE body loses its trailing period in the merged
      *  source, breaking GnuCOBOL compilation.  ACCT-FIXTURE-001
      *  is referenced via depends_on_files schema and the same
      *  byte-derived value (numeric 1) is inlined here.
      *
      *  PERFORMs 3000-READ-ACCOUNT (CBTRN01C.cbl L241-250).  Line
      *  242 MOVEs ACCT-ID to FD-ACCT-ID.  Lines 243-250 are a
      *  READ ... INVALID KEY / NOT INVALID KEY / END-READ compound
      *  that cobol-check strips: BOTH arms' bodies remain as
      *  orphan code.  ACCT-ID is preserved through the paragraph
      *  (no orphan-body MOVE rewrites it), so the fixture-loaded
      *  value is observable post-PERFORM.
      *
      *  Source of expected value: ACCT-ID = '00000000001' is the
      *  byte-exact value of bytes 1-11 of acctdata.txt record 1;
      *  the alphanumeric form is required because cobol-check
      *  0.2.16 cannot resolve PIC 9(11) types declared inside a
      *  COPY'd copybook (CVACT01Y) and defaults to alphanumeric
      *  comparison; not recomputed.
      *  CEE3ABD verification: NEVER HAPPENED.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 3000-READ-ACCOUNT NOT INVALID KEY succeeds with fixture'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE 1 TO ACCT-ID
            PERFORM 3000-READ-ACCOUNT
            EXPECT ACCT-ID TO BE '00000000001'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC8 -- 3000-READ-ACCOUNT INVALID KEY sets WS-ACCT-READ-STATUS
      *         to 4
      *
      *  PERFORMs 3000-READ-ACCOUNT (CBTRN01C.cbl L241-250) with no
      *  fixture loaded.  Under cobol-check's READ-INVALID-KEY
      *  stripping, the INVALID KEY orphan body unconditionally
      *  runs production line 247: MOVE 4 TO WS-ACCT-READ-STATUS.
      *  This testcase asserts that side effect.  A pre-PERFORM
      *  sentinel (MOVE 9999) ensures the post-state is provably a
      *  production side effect, not an INITIALIZE residue.
      *
      *  Source of expected value: WS-ACCT-READ-STATUS = 4 is the
      *  production literal at L247 (inside 3000-READ-ACCOUNT's
      *  INVALID KEY arm), copied verbatim; not recomputed.
      *  CEE3ABD verification: NEVER HAPPENED.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 3000-READ-ACCOUNT INVALID KEY sets WS-ACCT-READ-STATUS to 4'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE 9999 TO WS-ACCT-READ-STATUS
            PERFORM 3000-READ-ACCOUNT
            EXPECT WS-ACCT-READ-STATUS TO BE 4
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC9 -- 9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE succeeds with status 00
      *
      *  PERFORMs 9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE (CBTRN01C.cbl L361-377) with
      *  DALYTRAN-STATUS = '00' to drive the SUCCESS branch:
      *  L362 ADD 8 TO ZERO GIVING APPL-RESULT (production verb,
      *  not test recomputation; AAP rule allows production verbs
      *  inside the paragraph under test); L363 CLOSE (stripped);
      *  L364 IF DALYTRAN-STATUS = '00' THEN L365 MOVE 0 TO
      *  APPL-RESULT; L369 IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE (exit).
      *
      *  Source of expected value: APPL-RESULT = 0 is the
      *  production literal at L365; not recomputed.
      *  CEE3ABD verification: NEVER HAPPENED.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE succeeds with status 00'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO DALYTRAN-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC10 -- Z-ABEND-PROGRAM invokes CEE3ABD stub
      *
      *  Z-ABEND-PROGRAM (CBTRN01C.cbl L469-473) is the LE-abend
      *  wrapper PERFORMed transitively from every error pathway.
      *  Production body: L470 DISPLAY 'ABENDING PROGRAM'; L471
      *  MOVE 0 TO TIMING; L472 MOVE 999 TO ABCODE; L473 CALL
      *  'CEE3ABD'.
      *
      *  This testcase MOCKs CALL 'CEE3ABD' so the LE service stub
      *  does not actually fire (the test process must survive),
      *  PERFORMs the wrapper paragraph, and asserts on:
      *    a. TIMING = 0 (production L471 MOVE literal).
      *    b. ABCODE = 999 (production L472 MOVE literal).
      *    c. CALL 'CEE3ABD' was invoked exactly once (VERIFY).
      *  Test setup MOVE 7777 TO ABCODE / MOVE 8888 TO TIMING
      *  ensures the post-state is provably a production side
      *  effect; if the production MOVEs fail to execute, the
      *  assertions on TIMING=0 / ABCODE=999 would fail.
      *
      *  Source of expected values: TIMING = 0 (L471), ABCODE = 999
      *  (L472).  Production literals; not recomputed.
      *  CEE3ABD verification: HAPPENED ONCE (the production CALL
      *  at L473 dispatches to the per-testcase mock once per
      *  PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C Z-ABEND-PROGRAM invokes CEE3ABD stub'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE 7777 TO ABCODE
            MOVE 8888 TO TIMING
            PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM
            EXPECT ABCODE TO BE 999
            EXPECT TIMING TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC11 -- Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS formats numeric status
      *
      *  PERFORMs Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS (CBTRN01C.cbl L476-489) with
      *  IO-STATUS = '23' to drive the ELSE arm: L477-478 IF
      *  IO-STATUS NOT NUMERIC OR IO-STAT1 = '9' [THEN: TWO-BYTES-
      *  BINARY pack] ELSE L485 MOVE '0000' TO IO-STATUS-04; L486
      *  MOVE IO-STATUS TO IO-STATUS-04(3:2); DISPLAY ...; END-IF;
      *  L489 EXIT.
      *
      *  IO-STATUS = '23' is numeric (NOT NUMERIC false) and IO-
      *  STAT1 = '2' (not '9'), so the OR-guard evaluates false and
      *  the ELSE arm executes.  L485 MOVEs literal '0000' into
      *  IO-STATUS-04; L486 reference-modifies positions 3-4 with
      *  '23', yielding '0023'.  IO-STATUS = '23' is the canonical
      *  VSAM "record-not-found" status code per AAP Section 0.7.1.
      *
      *  Source of expected value: IO-STATUS-04 = '0023' is the
      *  production literal '0000' (L485) with the test-author
      *  IO-STATUS = '23' overlaid at positions 3-4 by the
      *  production reference-modified MOVE (L486); directly
      *  observable from the production MOVEs; not recomputed.
      *  CEE3ABD verification: NEVER HAPPENED.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS formats numeric status'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '23' TO IO-STATUS
            PERFORM Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS
            EXPECT IO-STATUS-04 TO BE '0023'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

